--- a/docs/develop/compiler.rst
+++ b/docs/develop/compiler.rst
@@ -203,6 +203,11 @@ The second and third passes involve computing the Python stack size and code siz
 for the bytecode or native code. After the third pass the code size cannot change,
 otherwise jump labels will be incorrect.
 
+For bytecode, stack sizing must also account for values retained during exception
+handling and unwinding. A ``finally`` block entered by a return or loop jump keeps
+both the return value or jump destination and an unwind sentinel on the stack,
+rather than the single ``None`` or exception used on other entry paths.
+
 .. code-block:: c
 
    for (scope_t *s = comp->scope_head; s != NULL && comp->compile_error == MP_OBJ_NULL; s = s->next) {
